+## Change log — 0.9.7_Hardened_1
+
+**0.9.7 is one owner-approved language change: the `@latebound` callable-type
+boundary, closing ODR-015.** It changes which callback-return and escape programs
+are accepted, which is why it is a language revision and not a hardening.
+
+*(Reconstructed by `0.9.7_Hardened_2` from the 0.9.7 Audit Record, the ODR-015
+ruling it cites, and a mechanical diff of the rule set. H1 recorded this work in
+audit rows and banner blocks and in no change log; the rows below are what
+the completeness rule `[DIA-6a]` requires.)*
+
+| # | Change | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **`@latebound` is admitted on a callable type** (`[FN-6b]`). `@latebound fn(Span[T]) -> R` supplies fresh invocation-local regions for its borrowed and view parameters. It is permitted only immediately before a callable type: it is not an item attribute, names no region, and appears in no runtime value, ABI byte, reload schema or source-visible lifetime identity. | V, III `fn_type` |
+| 2 | **The boundary's region rules** (`[LT-7]` amended, `[LT-8]`, `[LT-8a]`, `[LT-10]`). Each invocation binds fresh regions; the invocation's result MUST be free of them, so a callback cannot return or publish a view of what it was lent. Ordinary region and escape diagnostics remain authoritative — the boundary introduces no bespoke diagnostic and no compiler intrinsic. | XXIV §H14.3, VII |
+| 3 | **The fact is part of compile-time callable identity** (`[FN-6a]`, `[FN-6]` amended). `@latebound` participates in canonical type identity, generic substitution, expected-callable checking, interface/EMIF compatibility and incremental invalidation, and `Callable[Args, R]` preserves it rather than erasing it. | V |
+| 4 | **`std.borrow.with_views*` stays an ordinary library API.** No compiler recognition of those names is permitted; the helpers are ordinary functions whose callback parameters are spelled `@latebound`. This is what keeps the feature reusable rather than a special case for one module. | XXIV §H14.3 |
+| 5 | **Version selection** (`[MOD-6]` amended, `[MOD-6a]`). `0.9.7` selects the `@latebound` contract; `0.9`, `0.9.5` and `0.9.6` do not silently acquire it. | V |
+| 6 | **Conformance** (`[TST-20]`, `[TST-21]` amended): adversarial escape, storage, owned-capture, FFI-publication, freshness and nested-boundary cases. | XXIV §MRV-8 |
+| 7 | No diagnostic code is added. `@latebound` violations are reported by the existing region and escape diagnostics, which is the design. | — |
+
+**Evidence.** `@latebound` is **SPECIFIED**, not implemented or conformant. H1's
+Evidence Status section states the condition and it is unchanged.
