+## Change log — 0.9.5
+
+**0.9.5 is one language change — inferred multi-region `@view` structs — plus ten
+hardenings that completed the callback-composition and Arena-initialisation
+contracts around it.**
+
+*(Reconstructed by `0.9.7_Hardened_2` from the 0.9.5_Hardened_1–10 audit records
+and the owner rulings they cite.)*
+
+| # | Change | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **Inferred multi-region views** (`[LT-14]`..`[LT-43]`, `[TYP-15]`, `[TYP-15a]`, `[LT-2]` amended). A `@view struct` may carry any finite number of independently inferred borrow regions in a compiler-internal **region vector**, one slot per borrowed field. `[LT-16]` preserves each field's provenance instead of intersecting; `[LT-17]` makes validity **conjunctive** — a view is usable only while every slot a reachable field needs is valid — and that is the safety core of the feature. `[LT-15]` forbids requiring any named-lifetime syntax; `[LT-30]` keeps region slots out of the runtime representation, so two instantiations differing only in region have identical size, alignment, offsets, padding and calling convention. `[LT-31a]` keeps region identity out of *nominal* type identity — two values of one `@view struct` with different region vectors share a type, an ABI, a symbol and a layout descriptor, so the feature causes no monomorphisation or vtable bloat — and `[LT-34]` preserves every legacy one-region program. | XXIV §MRV, IV, VII |
