+## Reference-compiler model and boundaries
+
+The three sections below were carried under the *0.9.6_Hardened_1 Simplicity-Consolidation Record*
+in `0.9.7_Hardened_1`. That record's narrative — version treatment, amendment classes, source and
+authority — is provenance and sits in Appendix H; these three sections are contract and sit here.
+`0.9.7_Hardened_2` added this one heading so that they have a parent in this Part. Their text is
+unchanged.
+
+### Consolidated reference-compiler model
+
+The reference compiler is organized around reusable facts rather than feature-specific safety
+systems:
+
+```text
+TypeIdentity
+BorrowCapability
+OwnershipGraph
+AccessContract
+InitializationState
+LayoutDescriptor
+EffectSet
+```
+
+`BorrowCapability` conceptually keeps lifetime provenance separate from concrete storage identity,
+and keeps each of access permission, representation kind, ownership relation, acquisition/checking,
+unsafe authority, synchronization, validity, and escape constraints on an independent axis. A raw
+pointer is a representation kind, not an access permission; a mutable raw pointer combines mutable
+permission with raw-pointer representation and an unsafe authority boundary. Escape constraints are
+a set/predicate rather than one mutually exclusive enum.
+
+Feature-specific semantics remain distinct applications of those facts. Arena is a region allocator,
+not an interior-mutability primitive. `Cell`, `RefCell`, synchronization guards, and `UnsafeCell`
+retain their different authority and runtime invariants. ECS remains library-owned. Foreign calls
+remain contract-driven. Coroutines do not acquire an escape exemption. Shared machinery never
+generalizes H10's dynamic class-exclusivity policy into ordinary borrow checking.
+
+### Preservation boundaries
+
+The consolidation preserves three intentionally different replacement paths:
+
+```text
+ordinary assignment:          evaluate new -> drop old live value -> store new
+Cell.set:                     evaluate/receive new -> store new -> drop old
+MaybeUninit.write/write_at:   evaluate/receive new -> store new -> do not drop prior bytes
+```
+
+It also preserves H10's mandatory cycle diagnostics, exact/declared/unknown callable-access model,
+field-to-region provenance summaries, conservative opaque-call behavior, summary invalidation,
+FFI exception policy, and runtime erasure of compiler-only region/capability metadata.
+
+### Evidence boundary
+
+This file specifies the target architecture. It does not establish that the current compiler uses the
+canonical facts, implements 0.9.5 multi-region views, or passes the target's conformance conditions.
+Existing conformance-backed behavior, specified-but-unimplemented behavior, and current divergences
+remain separate evidence classes. The current compiler is not an oracle for rules it has not
+implemented; differences are classified against this specification and owner decisions.
+
