+#### 0.9.6_Hardened_5 language-conformance condition
+
+`0.9.6_Hardened_5` MUST NOT be declared conformant until all H1 through H4 conditions remain satisfied and
+repository evidence additionally proves that:
+
+1. equivalent borrow relationships represented by `Span`, `MutSpan`, `ref`, `ref mut`, `@view`
+   fields, Arena-backed views, `RefCell` guards, and foreign views receive equivalent safety decisions
+   where their semantic axes are equivalent;
+2. lifetime provenance and concrete storage identity remain distinct, and neither region equality nor
+   region inequality is used as a substitute for an overlap/disjointness proof;
+3. exact, trusted-declared, and conservative-unknown callable facts preserve both access and
+   field-to-region provenance, including generic, separately compiled, dynamic, and hot-reload target
+   sets;
+4. changing either callable summary rechecks affected callers and invalidates all dependent interface,
+   generic, and cache artifacts; stale metadata is a hard compiler failure;
+5. compiler-only capability, region, access-summary, and initialization-proof metadata is absent from
+   runtime layout, ABI, serialization, and hot-reload schemas;
+6. ordinary assignment, `Cell.set`, and `MaybeUninit.write`/`write_at` preserve their distinct ordering
+   contracts in MIR and generated code;
+7. `[ARN-10]` tests show successful `Default` construction, v1 process termination through `[PAN-1]`
+   on panic, no continuation after panic, no compiler-invented unwind path, and no observation of
+   post-panic Arena state;
+8. existing H10/H1/H2 safety regressions remain present and green; implementation-path consolidation is
+   not used to delete an adversarial test;
+9. `[TST-24]` proves empty fixed-capacity construction, exact Arena provenance, no post-construction
+   allocation/cursor movement, `CapacityError.Full`, complete Array/Map operations, drop-free bounds,
+   ordinary borrow conflicts, named iterator contracts, deterministic iteration requirements, and
+   generic substitution;
+10. `[HASH-1]`–`[HASH-4]` are implemented through the ordinary interface/type machinery, equal
+    values produce equal hashes, supplied spans cannot escape the hasher call, `finish` consumes its
+    move-only state, custom Map keys satisfy `Eq + Hash`, and no safe Map API exposes mutable keys;
+11. implementation and conformance evidence does not freeze `DefaultHasher`'s current mixing
+    algorithm as source-level behavior;
+12. ODR-013's statically generic `H: Hasher` representation is reflected consistently in signatures,
+    inference, monomorphization, implementation, and conformance without bare-interface or
+    compiler-only dynamic coercion.
+13. every `CallInfo`-style aggregate, cache, index, summary, and serialized compiler artifact is
+    derived from authoritative semantic facts, invalidated with them, and rejected when stale;
+14. `AccessContract`, `EffectSet`, provenance, retention, storage identity, permission,
+    representation, ownership, checking, unsafe authority, synchronization, validity, escape, and
+    initialization remain independent wherever H4 distinguishes them;
+15. initialization analysis retains `Uninit | Maybe | Init` plus required field/element/range facts,
+    and no unknown fact becomes a capability or definite-uninitialized proof;
+16. same-Arena distinct allocations retain distinct storage identities, unknown overlap never emits
+    `noalias`, and unknown callable/foreign/dynamic boundaries use their domain's conservative result;
+17. no `Len`/`Capacity` interface, parallel safety system, automatic dynamic-borrow fallback, or
